Backport of the fix for a use-after-free with duplicate XML entities in the
bundled copy of librsvg.

Upstream fix:
  https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/librsvg/-/merge_requests/1222
  commit 1606574427408baca8203ef723281509a229f9e2
  "(#1241): Fix use-after-free with duplicate XML entities"
  Fixes https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/librsvg/-/work_items/1241

When an included XML document declares an entity whose name duplicates an
already-declared one, librsvg freed the old xmlEntityPtr while libxml2 still
held and used pointers to it. The fix ignores entity declarations whose name
is already present. Entity creation is moved into XmlState::entity_insert so
the duplicate is never even created.

Adapted to the bundled librsvg 2.58.0: upstream was written against 2.60,
whose entity HashMap stores an XmlEntity Drop wrapper. In 2.58 the HashMap
stores raw XmlEntityPtr values that are freed explicitly (in entity_insert on
replace, and in build_document on teardown), so the duplicate-free happened in
entity_insert directly rather than via Drop. The backport keeps 2.58's raw
pointer storage and only applies the behavioural change (skip duplicates).

